Chapter: X509ConstraintsTest
  cites Encode chapter X509Chain
  cites Encode chapter X509
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 ECDSA P-256 chains made by .NET CertificateRequest on 2026-10-07, valid 2026-01-01 to 2036-01-01, all under the
 self-signed "SigSlip Root" (the anchor). .NET X509Chain with that root as its only trust anchor accepts chain A and
 refuses B (InvalidBasicConstraints), C (NotValidForUsage), D (HasNotPermittedNameConstraint) and E
 (HasNotSupportedCriticalExtension). A: leaf, intermediate. B: leaf, a CA, the CA's issuer with pathLenConstraint 0.
 C: leaf, an issuer whose critical keyUsage is digitalSignature only. D: a leaf for evil.test, an issuer with a
 critical nameConstraints permitting only ok.test. E: a leaf carrying the critical extension 1.3.6.1.4.1.99999.1,
 the intermediate of A.

